    <tags>chess tui console game chess-engines unicode</tags>
    <summary>TUI chess in Java</summary>
    <description>Play chess in your terminal against a choice of AI engines.

Console Chess draws the board with Unicode chess glyphs, so it renders in any modern terminal (Windows Terminal, VT-enabled consoles, macOS and Linux). Move the cursor with the arrow keys or hjkl, select and confirm moves with Enter/Space, and quit with q.

Four engines ship behind one interface: noise (default, ELO ~750-1250), greedy (ELO ~500), adam (minimax with piece-square tables, ELO ~1600) and stockfish (Stockfish over UCI, Elo-capped 1350-2800, installed automatically as a dependency).

Run console-chess -e engine -d easy|medium|hard to pick an engine and difficulty.</description>
    <releaseNotes>__RELEASE_URL__</releaseNotes>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="stockfish" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
</package>
